    "title": "Crews investigate NE OKC house fire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "OKLAHOMA CITY ( KFOR ) — The Oklahoma City Fire Department responded to a house fire in Northeast Oklahoma City on Wednesday night. Authorities arrived at the scene to heavy smoke and flames coming from the front of the home at northeast 14th Street and north Bath Avenue. The fire was knocked out quickly and officials say that no injuries have been reported. The scene of the fire is under further investigation. The estimated cost of damages is 40K-50K. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KFOR.com Oklahoma City.",
